<Database>
    <LocalizedText>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_MOD_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Economics</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_MOD_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Borrow from other civilizations or a bond market and pay it back from what the Gold brings in, lend to a neighbour in trouble, pick a tax level as a policy card, and watch an auto-loan guard keep you clear of the game's negative-balance penalties. Missed payments cost you, default costs more, and repudiating a debt keeps the Gold at the price of your name. Single-player.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Loans</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Whether civilizations can borrow from each other and, later, from a bond market, within a limit set by income. Off turns the loans off; trade bills and investment keep their own options.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Nobody borrows or lends, and the guard stays out.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_LOANS_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Loans between civilizations open with Moneylending, the bond market with Public debt.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Auto-loan guard</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>When your treasury is about to fall below the line where the game starts taking amenities, the guard takes out an emergency loan for you, up to a cap of ten turns of your income. You can also switch it on the Loans tab.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>You borrow only when you ask to. The game's penalties for a negative balance apply as usual.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_GUARD_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>An emergency loan covers a shortfall before the game's penalties start, until the cap is reached. You're told once when it is.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>AI borrowing and lending</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Whether the computer players take part: borrowing when they run short, lending when they're flush, restructuring an overdue loan, and now and then repudiating a debt to an enemy.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Only you borrow and lend. The computer players keep their treasuries as the base game runs them.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_AI_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Computer players borrow, lend, restructure and repudiate by the same rules you play under.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Rates</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Scales every interest rate in the game, the rate cap included. Standard is 3 percent a turn in Antiquity, 2 in Exploration and 1.5 in Modern before standing and relationship adjust it.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_LOW" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Low</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_LOW_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Three quarters of the standard rates. Borrowing is cheap and lending pays less.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_STANDARD" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Standard</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_STANDARD_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>The rates the mod is balanced around.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_HIGH" Language="fr_FR"><Text>High</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_RATES_HIGH_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>A quarter above the standard rates. Debt bites sooner and lending pays more.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Taxes</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Adds the tax policy cards: Light Taxation, Heavy Taxation and War Levy. Each trades Gold against happiness in one of your ordinary policy slots, and the computer players choose among them as they do any card.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>The tax cards aren't in the game.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TAXES_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>The three tax cards appear in the policy list as their civics unlock them.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Economic stages</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Whether each part opens with the tech or civic that historically brought it in: loans between civilizations with Moneylending, the bond market and longer terms with Public debt.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Every part is open from the start of its age.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_STAGES_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>A part opens for a civilization when it reaches the stage's tech or civic. With the option off everything is open from the start of its age.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Markets and trade bills</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Gives every resource a world price, set by how many copies there are and who needs them. Each pair of civilizations then settles the net value of what they import from each other every turn, and a civilization pays at most a tenth of its income this way.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Resources have no price, and a route costs the importer what it does in the base game.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_MARKETS_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Bills open with the Trade stage (Code of Laws in Antiquity) and show on the Trade tab.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Tariffs</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Lets a civilization hold back part of what it owes the civilizations it imports from: 10 percent at Low, 25 at High. A High tariff costs relationship with each partner it bills. Needs Markets and trade bills.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Every civilization pays its full bill.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_TARIFFS_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Tariffs open with Imperialism, on the Fiscal tab. The computer players answer a High tariff in kind.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Foreign investment</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Lets civilizations put Gold into each other: a development loan on a city's current build, a general investment in its treasury, or either as aid with nothing asked back.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_OFF" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Off</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_OFF_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Each civilization keeps its Gold at home.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_ON" Language="fr_FR"><Text>On</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_SETUP_INVESTMENT_ON_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Development loans open with Guild patronage (Guilds), general investment with Chartered companies (Colonialism), and aid is open from the start.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_LIGHT_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Light Taxation</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_LIGHT_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>-2 Gold and +4 Happiness in each settlement.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_HEAVY_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>Heavy Taxation</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_HEAVY_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>+4 Gold and -2 Happiness in each settlement.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_WAR_LEVY_NAME" Language="fr_FR"><Text>War Levy</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_CARD_WAR_LEVY_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>While you're at war: +8 Gold and -4 Happiness in each settlement. In peacetime it doesn't pay or cost anything.</Text></Replace>
        <Replace Tag="LOC_ECONOMICS_TAX_SLOT_DESCRIPTION" Language="fr_FR"><Text>+1 Policy slot, for a tax card or any other.</Text></Replace>
